[[B-embedding-git-in-your-applications]]
[appendix]
== Embedding Git in your Applications

If you are building a tool for designers—like the SketchSpark app—chances are good that you need to handle versions, parallel explorations, and team synchronization. Instead of reinventing the wheel, you can use Git as your application's "versioning engine."

Many modern design tools (like Figma, Abstract, or Kactus) use Git or Git-like models under the hood. In this appendix, we’ll look at the technical ways you can integrate Git directly into your own software, from simple command-line automation to embedding high-performance libraries like **Libgit2**.

